.TH CALIBRATE 1 "12 October 2026" Linux "FPAC Operator's Manual"
.SH NAME
calibrate \- transmitter test pattern generator.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B calibrate [-t seconds] port
.SH DESCRIPTION
.LP
.B calibrate
sends 100 UI frames of 128 bytes to an AX.25 port, from the callsign of the
port to the callsign TEST, to test a TNC/Radio. Each frame carries a three
digit frame number followed by ASCII U (01010101) characters. It stops by
itself after the last frame.
.P
The port must be configured (ie with kissattach) before it can be used. 
.SH OPTIONS
.TP 13
.BI "\-t  seconds "
Time between two frames, in seconds. Default 1 (the whole test then lasts
about 100 seconds). Decimals are allowed, down to 0.01.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP 13
.BI CR
Stop transmitting.
.SH BUGS
.P
If the paclen of the port in axports is less than 128 you will get an error
message for each frame. Until 4.1.6-rc7 the program read \-t in milliseconds,
although this page said seconds.
.SH SEE ALSO
/usr/local/share/doc/fpac/calibrate.txt
